title: Vocabulary - Fountain
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Reference for [[vocab/fountain]], a Custom-Markup vocabulary for screenplay-style content in the spirit of https://fountain.io/syntax/. Worked example: [[Example - Fountain screenplay]].

!! Activation

`type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Fountain` on a tiddler. Activate WITHOUT Default if you want the forced-scene `.<text>` marker to fire (it collides with vocab/default's DOT).

When activated, the vocab declares:

* `disable-core-rules: heading list` so `!action`, `*` / `**` / `#` / `;` / `:` / `>` line-starts belong to Fountain instead of TW core.
* `front-matter: yes` so a `Key: Value` block at the very top of the tiddler renders as a title page (terminated by a blank line or `===`).

Other TW rules stay active: `[[Other tiddler]]` prettylinks, `<<macros>>`, tables, `''bold''` / `//italic//` / `__underline__` TW emphasis still work. See [[Vocabulary Engine]] for the `disable-core-rules`, `front-matter`, and per-marker mechanisms used here.

!! Marker map

|! Element |! Fountain |! Marker |
|''Title page'' | `Key: Value` lines at top | (handled by the `frontmatter` wikirule, not a marker) |
|Fade in (opener) |`FADE IN:` |[[vocab/fountain/FADE-IN]] |
|Fade out |`FADE OUT.` |[[vocab/fountain/FADE-OUT]] |
|Cut to |`CUT TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/CUT-TO]] |
|Dissolve to |`DISSOLVE TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/DISSOLVE-TO]] |
|Smash cut to |`SMASH CUT TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/SMASH-CUT-TO]] |
|Match cut to |`MATCH CUT TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/MATCH-CUT-TO]] |
|Wipe to |`WIPE TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/WIPE-TO]] |
|Iris in |`IRIS IN:` |[[vocab/fountain/IRIS-IN]] |
|Iris out |`IRIS OUT:` |[[vocab/fountain/IRIS-OUT]] |
|Interior scene |`INT. LOCATION - TIME` |[[vocab/fountain/INT]] |
|Exterior scene |`EXT. LOCATION - TIME` |[[vocab/fountain/EXT]] |
|Interior/exterior |`I/E. LOCATION` |[[vocab/fountain/I-E]] |
|Establishing |`EST. LOCATION` |[[vocab/fountain/EST]] |
|Forced character |`@ NAME` (one line) |[[vocab/fountain/CHARACTER]] |
|Forced action |`! action` |[[vocab/fountain/ACTION]] |
|Forced scene |`. scene` |[[vocab/fountain/SCENE]] |
|Synopsis |`= text` |[[vocab/fountain/SYNOPSIS]] |
|Section header |`# Section`, `## Sub`, ...  |[[vocab/fountain/SECTION]] |
|Centered text |`> centered <` |[[vocab/fountain/CENTERED]] |
|Italic |`*italic*` |[[vocab/fountain/ITALIC]] |
|Bold |`**bold**` |[[vocab/fountain/BOLD]] |
|Bold italic |`***bold italic***` |[[vocab/fountain/BOLD-ITALIC]] |
|Underline |`_underline_` |[[vocab/fountain/UNDERLINE]] |
|Boneyard |`/* ... */` |[[vocab/fountain/BONEYARD]] |

!! What works

* Title page: `Title:`, `Credit:`, `Author:` etc. at the top of the tiddler, terminated by a blank line or `===`.
* Scene headings: `INT.` / `EXT.` / `I/E.` / `EST.` keep their prefix visible in the rendered output.
* Transitions: keyword stays visible (`CUT TO:`, `FADE IN:`, ...). `FADE IN:` is left-aligned (opener convention); other transitions are right-aligned.
* Character cues: `@ NAME` on its own line renders as a centered uppercase paragraph. Dialogue lines that follow render as regular paragraphs.
* Synopsis (`= text`), Boneyard (`/* ... */`), Action (`! ...`), Section (`# heading`), Centered (`> text <`), inline emphasis (`*italic*`, `**bold**`, `***bold italic***`, `_underline_`).

!! Known limitations

* ''Dialogue auto-styling.'' Fountain renders dialogue paragraphs (the lines following a character cue) with a narrower indent. The marker engine has no lookahead, so dialogue after `@ NAME` renders as a regular paragraph rather than dialogue-styled. Tracked in beads; no current workaround beyond styling specific paragraphs by hand.
* ''Parentheticals.'' Fountain's `(closer)` between a character cue and a dialogue line gets its own indent in real screenplays. Same lookahead constraint as dialogue; not supported.
* ''Whitespace after the glyph.'' Glyph markers (`@`, `!`, `=`, `.`) require a whitespace after the literal. Fountain's spec-style `@NAME` does not fire; use `@ NAME` instead.
* ''Source-bolded transitions.'' Some Fountain authors write `**FADE IN:**` (with bold delimiters) in source to make the opener stand out in plain-text editors. In vocab/fountain the inline `**...**` bold marker fires first and wraps the line as `<strong>`, so the block-level FADE-IN word marker never matches. Write the bare form `FADE IN:` (without surrounding `**`) to get the transition styling. Same for any other transition wrapped in source emphasis.
* ''Multi-line title page values.'' The front-matter parser is intentionally simple and only understands one-line `Key: Value` pairs. Fountain's spec also allows multi-line values via leading-whitespace continuation (e.g. `Notes:\n\tfirst line\n\tsecond line`); ours doesn't. Restructure as one-line values or accept that continuation lines fall out of the title-page block.
* ''Auto character detection.'' Fountain detects "ALL-CAPS line followed by dialogue" as an implicit character cue; we require the explicit `@ NAME` form.
* ''The `.` forced-scene marker'' collides with vocab/default's `DOT`. Activate Fountain ''without'' Default if you need it.
* ''The `>` / `<` centered marker'' uses Fountain's literal characters; tiddlers that mix inequality-style text (`if a > b then`) can hit false matches. Screenplay contexts are usually safe.

